      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "****UNDER OFFER****\r\n\r\nStep into a piece of local history with this enchanting detached streetside bungalow. Combining early 20th-century character with a prime village location, this c.1930 masonry-built home stands proudly on a prominent corner site along the N69. Ready to welcome its next chapter, it is the perfect find for first-time buyers, downsizers, or anyone looking for a property with genuine soul and convenience.\r\n\r\nTimeless Character & Kerb Appeal\r\n•\tStunning Facade: Features a classic brown pebble-dash finish, perfectly accented by vibrant white and reddish-pink painted trim around the windows and entryway.\r\n•\tArchitectural Flair: Crowned by a traditional hip-style slate roof and flanked by two prominent, light-filled bay windows that frame the central entrance.\r\n•\tOrnate Welcome: A beautiful, arched porch with decorative white moulding offers an elegant, character-rich first impression.\r\nBright, Functional Living Spaces.\r\n\r\nThe interior layout maximizes light and comfort, offering a practical layout that comprises:\r\n•\tWelcoming entrance hallway.\r\n•\tGenerous front sitting room illuminated by the bay window.\r\n•\t2 comfortable bedrooms.\r\n•\tCozy living/dining area ideal for relaxing evenings.\r\n•\tNeat kitchenette and a practical shower room\r\n\r\nSun-Drenched Outdoor Spaces\r\n•\tGated Access: Secure, pedestrian gates on both sides of the property lead effortlessly around the home.\r\n•\tSunny Aspect: A private rear courtyard and a lovely front garden command an excellent sun orientation, perfect for outdoor dining or low-maintenance gardening.\r\n\r\nAn Unbeatable Village Location\r\nSituated in the historic village of Tarbert, you are just a short stroll from local schools, shops, traditional pubs, and the scenic Shannon estuary ferry connection. Everything you need is right on your doorstep.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly advised to fully appreciate the warmth, character, and potential of this village gem."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - 1.5m x 4.6m \r\nVinyl flooring and ceiling coving.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.9m x 4.5m \r\nVinyl flooring, ceiling coving, hot-press and feature bay window overlooking front garden.\r\n\r\nSitting Room - 3.8m x 4.7m \r\nFitted carpet, ceiling coving, ornate fireplace with piped gas insert and feature bay window overlooking front garden. \r\n\r\nDining  Room - 4.3m x 3.5m \r\nVinyl flooring and oil  range - no longer in use.\r\n\r\nKitchenette - 2.7m x 2.0m \r\nVinyl flooring, dual aspect, fully fitted kitchenette with free stand electric oven, stainless steel sink, plumbed for dishwasher and rear door access.\r\n\r\nBathroom - 2.4m x 2.8m \r\nFully tiled floor to ceiling, wc, whb, Triton shower, timber latted ceiling, heated towel rail and large frosted window.\r\n\r\nInternal Corridor - 1.2m x 1.9m \r\nVinyl flooring and Stira to attic. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 4.0m x 3.1m \r\nVinyl flooring, ceiling coving, whb and window overlooking rear court yard.\r\n\r\nLock up store - 4.0m x 4.8m \r\nWith pedestrian access, lean to block built lock-up store with corrugated roof concrete floor, plumbed for washer n dryer and electricity.\r\n\r\nCovered Storage Area - 1.5m x 5.0m \r\nCovered with a canopy and houses the oil boiler and gas tank.  \r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
